From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "NickLabs Orbis (port)" <orbis@nicklabs.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:59:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu/ps4_bridge: display robustness knobs, enable
 retries, DP retrain, status

Ports the community MN864729 (CUH-12xx/Belize) display work from the linux-psx
7.2-ps4 series (rmux: 0051 DPCD-gated detect + polling, 0052, 0061, 0075 post-enable
retrain, 0078/0088 bounded enable retries, 0102 bridge reset between attempts, 0112
DPCD readiness wait, 0132 fixed-link CR/EQ poll bypass) onto 6.15.4, each behind a
parameter whose default keeps the Orbis 0.2.0 behaviour:

  amdgpu.ps4_bridge_dpcd_detect=1      connected = TMONREG HPD && DPCD read ok
  amdgpu.ps4_bridge_poll=1             DRM connector polling (no HPD irq on Belize)
  amdgpu.ps4_bridge_enable_attempts=N  1..5 MN864729 enable attempts, reset between
  amdgpu.ps4_bridge_dpcd_wait_ms=N     wait for DPCD before enabling
  amdgpu.ps4_bridge_retrain=1          DPCD refresh + DP retrain after enable
  amdgpu.ps4_bridge_extra_modes=1      also offer 1280x720@60 as a fallback mode
  amdgpu.ps4_dp_fixed_link=1           skip CR/EQ status polls (MN864729 only)

The MN864729 video sequence is unchanged; it moved into a helper so it can be retried.
New debugfs file dri/N/ps4_bridge_status reports the last enable result, attempts,
counters, TMONREG, DPCD result and the active knobs (read by orbis-debug).

Status: applies to 6.15.4 crashnt-4.7 + Orbis 0001 + 0101; not compiled or tested on
hardware by NickLabs Orbis.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/atombios_dp.c |  29 ++
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/ps4_bridge.c  | 346 ++++++++++++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 298 insertions(+), 77 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/atombios_dp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/atombios_dp.c
